.TH CYAML_DECLARE_SCOPED 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cyaml_declare_scoped \- declare a cyaml variable with automatic RAII destruction
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cyaml.h>

cyaml_declare_scoped(var_name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Declare a cyaml handle variable named var_name, set it to NULL and
attach a cleanup attribute to it.  When var_name goes out of scope, the
cleanup frees the tree that the variable holds recursively, exactly as
cyaml_destroy() does, and leaves the variable NULL.

The cleanup runs at the end of the enclosing block, in the reverse of
the declaration order, whether the block exits normally or through
break, continue, return or goto.

This is a GCC and Clang extension, which MSVC does not have.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
var_name  Name of the variable to declare.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
{
    cyaml_declare_scoped(doc);
    doc = cyaml_parse("x: 1\en", NULL);
    if (!doc) return;
    /* ... use doc ... */
}  /* doc is freed automatically here */
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_declare (3),
.BR cyaml_destroy (3)
